{"regla":"Mi regla en español"}

Allowed values, written exactly as they appear here:
- kind: TIMED, PRACTICE.
- paper: RUOE, WRITING, or null.
- part: positive integer, or null.
- source: LIBRO.
- category: PHRASAL_VERB.

Add the optional keys cause (CONFUSION) and confidence (SEGURO) to an error ONLY if I have stated them explicitly for that error. Don't infer them from the type of mistake or from a wrong answer; if they are missing, the form will suggest DESCONOCIMIENTO and DUDABA and I will review them.

WHAT YOU MUST NOT MAKE UP

A made-up value can't be told apart from a real one and stays in my history. When in doubt, leave "" or null.

- Don't make up a page, unit, paper, part, sourceRef, itemsTotal, itemsCorrect or anything about timing. Keep the session details I give you exactly as they are.
- Don't infer paper or part from the type of exercise. Work out itemsCorrect only if the whole session is there with all its errors.
- Transcribe myAnswer exactly, with its original spelling: don't correct it when you copy it.
- correctAnswer can only come from the answer key or a visible correction. If there is none, leave it as "".
- Include only what I point out, what is marked as wrong or what you can check against a reliable correction. Don't turn every exercise in the photo into an error.
- If some text can't be read clearly, leave it as "" so I can review it. Never write "illegible" or "pending" instead.
- If you can't tell what I got wrong, ask me for my answers, the answer key or a better screenshot before generating anything.

READING AND DETAIL

- Match each answer to its exercise number and its prompt, keeping gaps, punctuation and spelling.
- prompt holds the text needed to understand the error, with its options or instructions if they are needed.
- ruleNote explains in Spanish, briefly and concretely, the rule or criterion that stops the error from happening again: at least 15 characters and not just a repeat of correctAnswer. If you can't justify a useful rule, leave it as "".
- subcategory narrows down the category when it adds something; otherwise, "".
- itemRef is the identifier as it appears. Two different activities can repeat a number: keep each one's and tell them apart by the prompt.
- If several screenshots overlap, include each error only once. At most 120 errors per session.

Session details and corrections (text or attached images):
